{"article_ids": ["82ddf8032505d140"], "canonical_title": "Assurance-Conditioned Continuous Authorization for Autonomous AI Agents", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "The paper introduces Assurance-Conditioned Continuous Authorization (ACCA), a tool‑agnostic approach that maintains operational authority for autonomous software agents as they use tools, delegate tasks, or modify their models and execution environments. ACCA separates evidence validity from contextual applicability and derives assurance claims to decide whether current authorizations remain justified.", "entities": ["term:acca"], "first_seen": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_82ddf8032505d140", "importance_score": 5.84, "last_updated": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["59b285913cc2d8dc", "83d7690781e8e88d"], "canonical_title": "How Bayer Crop Science built an agentic decision engine on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore with AWS Unified Operations", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "U Mobile, Malaysia's newest 5G provider, built AiDaH, an agentic AI operations platform using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. The system moves beyond assistance to autonomous actions across telco operations. Nine months after launch it handles more than 150 operational scenarios in six divisions and has reduced trouble tickets by as much as 84.5%.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:ade", "term:aws"], "first_seen": "2026-10-23T16:21:36Z", "id": "evt_59b285913cc2d8dc", "importance_score": 5.74, "last_updated": "2026-11-04T16:23:33Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["3161d120c26a870c"], "canonical_title": "CARTBench: Rubric-Based Evaluation of Shopping Advice for Complex and Ambiguous Requests with Timelines", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Researchers released CARTBench, a rubric‑based benchmark that curates 1,603 product records and timestamped multi‑turn dialogues drawn from real commercial shopping needs across 17 retail domains, to evaluate large language model shopping assistants on complex and ambiguous requests with timelines.", "entities": ["term:cart"], "first_seen": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_3161d120c26a870c", "importance_score": 5.49, "last_updated": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["20366c4b5aede877"], "canonical_title": "Four layers of context engineering for production AI agents: How Deep Insight applies them in working code", "category": "open_source", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "Deep Insight published a four‑layer context engineering framework—covering architecture, prompts, file‑based tools, and verification agents—to address context‑management bottlenecks in production AI agents. The framework is delivered as working open‑source code built on the Strands Agents SDK and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore.", "entities": ["org:amazon"], "first_seen": "2026-11-04T16:30:40Z", "id": "evt_20366c4b5aede877", "importance_score": 5.195, "last_updated": "2026-11-04T16:30:40Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["a0ba445070c2b1fe"], "canonical_title": "AGORA: Reliability-Aware Aggregation of LLM Judges via Item-Response Theory", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "The paper presents AGORA, a method that applies item‑response theory to combine multiple LLM judges, accounting for differing reliability among judges. It notes that current per‑item mean weighting treats weak and strong judges alike and that confusion‑table models like Dawid‑Skene must estimate per‑judge error tables, especially when validation sets contain only a few hundred items.", "entities": ["term:agora"], "first_seen": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_a0ba445070c2b1fe", "importance_score": 5.09, "last_updated": "2026-11-05T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
